From 9acdd7e8f6517aa95e988836e78c7a19ddea8134 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:31:45 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(post): Tormach lathe moves one axis at a time after
 G30 and leaves the stock before it

The first rapid after a G30 ran diagonally from the operator's stored
G30 to the section's start point, and the closing G30 ran diagonally
from the last retract. With G30 stored in front of the face on
centre, or beside the bar, those lines could cross the stock.

tormach-lathe.cps now approaches the first point after G30 X first,
then Z, when the point is outside the stock's diameter, and Z first
(to the point, or to the ClearancePlane for a point on the face), then
X, when it is in front of the face. Before each G30 the tool leaves +X
to the stock's diameter, then +Z to the face, so the control's own G30
line starts at the stock's outer corner. No stock, or no stated
clearance where one is needed, is refused by name. The mill post is
not changed.

Pinned by lathe_post_tormach_g30 (four tests, each mutation-checked);
the Tormach lathe goldens change only in these moves.

Fixes #1604

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL
